flowchart TD
    accTitle: Texture creation wrapper responsibilities
    accDescr: Texture initialization is direct on the server thread or when the compositor allows asynchronous creation; otherwise it is queued. Each backend selects its own texture storage.
    Resource[ImageTexture resource] -->|scene identity and properties| API[RenderingServer API]
    API -->|virtual dispatch| Dispatch[RenderingServerDefault texture wrapper]
    Dispatch -->|server thread OR async creation allowed| Direct[Direct initialization]
    Dispatch -->|otherwise| Queue[CommandQueueMT initialization]
    Direct --> Storage[Selected RendererTextureStorage]
    Queue --> Storage
    Storage --> RDStorage[RendererRD TextureStorage]
    Storage --> GLStorage[GLES3 TextureStorage]
    Storage --> Dummy[Dummy TextureStorage]
    GLStorage -->|GL allocation| GL[OpenGL / OpenGL ES]
    RDStorage -->|format metadata and texture views| Device[RenderingDevice texture creation]
    Device -->|validated native description| Driver[RenderingDeviceDriver]
    Driver -->|API allocation| Native[Native texture]
